    'title' => "Arsenal's return to the summit",
    'teaser' => "Arsenal's 2025/2026 Premier League triumph ended a 22-year wait and marked the culmination of a patient rebuilding project. A balanced squad, a clear tactical identity, and the maturity to handle pressure carried the club through a demanding campaign and restored the championship to north London.",
    'body' => "<p>Arsenal's 2025/2026 Premier League triumph ended a 22-year wait for the title and marked the culmination of a patient rebuilding project. Years of investment in young players, modern recruitment, and a clear footballing identity finally produced a side capable of sustaining a championship challenge from the opening weeks to the final run-in.</p>

<p>The team combined disciplined possession with aggressive pressing and a defence built to control matches rather than merely survive them. Established leaders guided a core of players who had developed together, while competition for places ensured that injuries and fixture congestion did not derail the campaign. Important victories against direct rivals strengthened belief inside the squad and convinced supporters that the long wait could truly end.</p>

<p>The title also reflected the relationship between the team and its supporters. The Emirates Stadium became an increasingly intense venue, with fans responding to a side that played with courage and resilience. Away support remained equally important during difficult stretches, helping the players recover from setbacks and maintain momentum when the pressure of the race was at its greatest.</p>

<p>Winning the league after more than two decades carried meaning beyond the trophy itself. It connected a new generation with the championship teams of the past while establishing a foundation for the future. Arsenal returned to the summit not through a single dramatic gamble, but through sustained planning, tactical evolution, and faith in a group that learned how to turn promise into achievement.</p>",
